  "id": "COMPOUND:1727 - PROTEIN:6138",
  "verbalization": "Castanospermine is shown to interact with the CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide. These compounds are all implicated in targeting the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, suggesting a potential pathway where Castanospermine may modulate the activity of this subunit through the enzyme it targets. The evidence indicates a chain of interactions where Castanospermine could influence the proteasome's function, potentially through the enzyme it interacts with, which is a known component of the proteasome. The scores from the paths suggest a consistent and plausible mechanistic link, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple compounds targeting the same subunit supports the hypothesis that Castanospermine may exert its effects through a shared pathway involving this enzyme.",
